@startuml Workflow Ambiguity - Two Parallel Paths
!theme plain
title <font size=24 color="#1565C0"><b>ORDER STATE MACHINE AMBIGUITY</b></font>\n<font size=14 color="#1976D2">Two Parallel Workflows Creating Confusion</font>

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000

skinparam swimlane {
    BorderColor #000000
}

|#E8F5E9| Frontend Flow (Contract-Aware)
|#FFEBEE| Webhook Flow (Direct DB)

|Frontend Flow (Contract-Aware)|
start
:Customer clicks Pay;

:StripeOrderController.createCheckoutSession();

:Dispatch StripeCheckoutSessionRequestEvent;

:StripeContractCreationHandler
**Creates Contract (DRAFT)**;
#C8E6C9:osc_payment_contract
state = DRAFT;

:StripeCheckoutSessionHandler
**Stores provider info**;
#C8E6C9:osc_payment_contract
OXPROVIDERORDERID = 'pi_xxx';

:Redirect to Stripe Checkout;

:Customer pays on Stripe;

:Return to shop;

:StripeCheckoutReturnHandler
**Validates payment**;

:PaymentAuthorizedEventHandler
**Transitions to PENDING**;
#C8E6C9:osc_payment_contract
state = PENDING;

:fulfillCondition('payment_authorized')
**All conditions met**;
#C8E6C9:osc_payment_contract
state = READY_TO_COMMIT;

:StripeOrderCreationHandler
**Creates OXID Order**;
#FFF3E0:oxorder
OXTRANSID = 'pi_xxx';

#C8E6C9:osc_payment_contract
state = COMMITTED
OXORDERID = 'order123';

:Customer sees Thank You page;

note right
  <font color="#2E7D32"><b>Contract State: COMMITTED</b></font>
  Order created, awaiting payment confirmation
  Contract knows order ID
end note

|Webhook Flow (Direct DB)|

:Stripe sends webhook
payment_intent.succeeded;

:WebhookController receives;

:WebhookProcessingService.processEvent();

#FFCDD2:Does NOT look up Contract!;

:findOrderByPaymentIntentId()
**Direct DB lookup**;
#FFF3E0:SELECT FROM oxorder
WHERE OXTRANSID = 'pi_xxx';

:updateOrderPaymentState()
**Direct SQL**;
#FFEBEE:UPDATE osc_payment_order_state
SET OXPAYMENTSTATE = 'paid';

:updateOrderPaidTimestamp()
**Direct SQL**;
#FFF3E0:UPDATE oxorder
SET OXPAID = NOW();

:updateOrderTransStatus()
**Direct SQL**;
#FFF3E0:UPDATE oxorder
SET OXTRANSSTATUS = 'OK';

#FFCDD2:Contract STILL COMMITTED!
Never transitioned to FULFILLED;

stop

|Frontend Flow (Contract-Aware)|
note right
  <font color="#C62828"><b>PROBLEM!</b></font>
  Contract state: COMMITTED (stuck!)
  Order state: paid (via direct SQL)

  **State Mismatch:**
  - Contract thinks: "awaiting fulfillment"
  - Order thinks: "paid"
  - osc_payment_order_state: "paid"

  **No ContractFulfilledEvent!**
  - Subscribers don't fire
  - Audit trail incomplete
  - State machine broken
end note

legend bottom
  |= Workflow |= Color |= What it Updates |
  | <#E8F5E9> Frontend | Green | Contract + Order (correct) |
  | <#FFEBEE> Webhook | Red | Order only (bypasses contract) |

  **THE AMBIGUITY:**
  Two different workflows update order state differently:
  1. Frontend: Contract-first, event-driven
  2. Webhook: Direct DB, bypasses contract

  **RESULT:**
  - Contract stuck in COMMITTED forever
  - Order marked as paid
  - State machine inconsistent
  - Tests verify the broken behavior as "correct"
endlegend

@enduml
